## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
**Part A — Why This Company Can Compound:**  
AI demand → increased data center spending → higher memory chip usage → MU invests in R&D and capacity → strengthens market share → reinforces pricing power.  

**Durability Verdict:** Strong, as MU’s position in AI-driven memory demand creates a self-reinforcing loop.  

**Part B — Capex Cycle Risk:**  
MU is fab-lite, dependent on foundries, with high inventory exposure. Its revenue concentration in data centers (vs consumer) mitigates some cyclicality but not entirely. Current CapEx cycle positioning is uncertain due to AI-driven demand growth.  

**Severity:** **HIGH** — MU’s reliance on cyclical memory markets and high inventory levels expose it to potential overcapacity risks.

